    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d579">

                <pb facs="0646" n="534" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg534"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/1150: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The President of the Technical Board</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Stevens</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harbin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-10-20T22:00:00+08:26"><hi rendition="#italic">October 20,
                                1919, 10 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 22, 12:06
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Practically all original members of Service Corps including Emerson declare that
                    they are done and will leave for the United States and ask to be relieved
                    quickly. They all declare with truth they enlisted for the war and have served a
                    year after close away <pb facs="0647" n="535" xml:id="pg535"/> from families and
                    at pecuniary loss, that their efforts are useless under existing arrangement,
                    their instructions and orders are in every way ignored by officials of the
                    railways. …</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stevens</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
